              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Sanskrit for a guest house, then the Sanskrit for a stay abroad, a journey."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: वर्तते",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वर्तते — vartate — \"is present, exists\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "vartate is the present of the root √vṛt, \"to turn, roll\", and then \"to proceed, take place, exist\" (MW). MW compares Latin vertere, \"to turn\", and German werden, \"to become\". It is the verb inside parivartayati, \"changes\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
